 scar.\n\n* WHERE...The Gold Mountain Burn Scar north of Ouray, particularly\nalong Highway 550 between Cutler Creek and Dexter Creek.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Multiple rounds of thunderstorms are possible today which\ncould lead to flash flooding and/or debris flows. Residents near\nthe Gold Mountain burn scar should prepare for potential debris\nflows moving through Cutler Creek and Dexter Creek. Be sure to stay\nup to date with information from local authorities.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The highest potential for flash flooding and debris flows will\nfall between 6 PM and midnight tonight.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-30T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.749c252b67b0841e39c4de4282c31d6e351e8b56.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.749c252b67b0841e39c4de4282c31d6e351e8b56.001.1"}}]}